formule delle dediche votive nella Grecia arcaica","Dubois, 1989, IGDS","Jeffery, Johnston, 1990, LSAG","Arena, 2002, IGASMG II²",[226,227,228,229,230,231],"VB5QSXQK","CXHAXNBQ","3N7Z6QX5","RWXNUFEX","QUWGZA84","65P7AM6N",[233,234,235,21,26,30,236,237,238,239,240,241,242,114],"isic004523","dedication by the akragantines to apollo at delphi",{"_":5},"agrigentum","agrigento","sicilia","phocis","delphi","archaeological museum of delphi","ancient greek",[],{"title":245,"body":246,"divs":247,"editions":266,"images":276,"handnote":277},"ISic004523. Dedication by the Akragantines to Apollo at Delphi","\u003Cdiv id=\"editions\">\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[Ἀ]κραγαντῖνοι τ[ο͂ι \u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"divine\" data-text=\"Ἀπό\n                    λο̄νι\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἀπό\n                    λο̄νι\">Ἀπό-]\u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>λο̄νι\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\">(vac.)\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[.]ΚΡΑΓΑΝΤΙΝΟΙΤ[...\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"divine\" data-text=\"Ἀπό\n                    λο̄νι\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἀπό\n                    λο̄νι\">...]\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>ΛΟ̄ΝΙ\u003C/span>\u003C/span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; \u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>  \u003Cspan>Text after Arena 2002 (IGASMG II² 94).\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"lines 1–2\">lines.1–2: \u003Cspan>Arena prints the dialectal form Ἀπόλο̄νι and regularises it as Ἀπόλλωνι.\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"lines 1–2\">  \u003Cspan>Because the original width of the base cannot be established, the restoration remains uncertain. Dubois 1989 records the alternatives τ[ῶι Ἀπόλ]λωνι and τ[ὸ ἄγαλμα τῶι Ἀπόλ]λωνι; Arena 2002 adopts the former.\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>The Akragantines [dedicated this] to Apollo.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>Bousquet tentatively dated the dedication to the second quarter of the 5th century BCE and suggested a connection with the establishment of democracy at Akragas after the fall of the tyranny and the death of Theron in 472 BCE. De Waele, drawing on \u003Ca href=\"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0545.tlg002.perseus-grc2:2.33/\" target=\"_blank\">Aelian, Varia Historia 2.33\u003C/a>, conjectured that the base may have supported the ivory statue of the river-god Akragas said to have been dedicated at Delphi by the Akragantines in commemoration of the advent of democracy in 471 BCE. Both historical identifications remain conjectural. Bousquet distinguished this smaller base from the other Akragantine dedication at Delphi, inv. 5098 (Dubois 182b).\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Bousquet 1959 149–150, fig. 4 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001375\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001375\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> De Waele 1971 39–40 no. 8, pl. 10 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002040\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002040\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Lazzarini 1976 905 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002517\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002517\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Dubois 1989 182a \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000187\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000187\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Jeffery and Johnston 1990 Addenda, 372 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000678\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000678\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Arena 2002 94 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001373\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001373\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\"> \u003Cp>Bousquet notes rho with a triangular loop and a tail, alpha with an oblique crossbar descending to the foot of the right hasta, lunate sigma, and nu with an oblique left hasta and an almost vertical right hasta.\u003C/p> Lines 1–2  18–21  \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. \u003C/div>",[248,251,254,257,260,263],{"id":249,"html":250},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[Ἀ]κραγαντῖνοι τ[ο͂ι \u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"divine\" data-text=\"Ἀπό\n                    λο̄νι\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἀπό\n                    λο̄νι\">Ἀπό-]\u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>λο̄νι\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\">(vac.)\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[.]ΚΡΑΓΑΝΤΙΝΟΙΤ[...\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"divine\" data-text=\"Ἀπό\n                    λο̄νι\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἀπό\n                    λο̄νι\">...]\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>ΛΟ̄ΝΙ\u003C/span>\u003C/span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; \u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>",{"id":252,"html":253},"apparatus","\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>  \u003Cspan>Text after Arena 2002 (IGASMG II² 94).\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"lines 1–2\">lines.1–2: \u003Cspan>Arena prints the dialectal form Ἀπόλο̄νι and regularises it as Ἀπόλλωνι.\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"lines 1–2\">  \u003Cspan>Because the original width of the base cannot be established, the restoration remains uncertain. Dubois 1989 records the alternatives τ[ῶι Ἀπόλ]λωνι and τ[ὸ ἄγαλμα τῶι Ἀπόλ]λωνι; Arena 2002 adopts the former.\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>",{"id":255,"html":256},"translation","\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>The Akragantines [dedicated this] to Apollo.\u003C/p>  ",{"id":258,"html":259},"commentary","\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>Bousquet tentatively dated the dedication to the second quarter of the 5th century BCE and suggested a connection with the establishment of democracy at Akragas after the fall of the tyranny and the death of Theron in 472 BCE. De Waele, drawing on \u003Ca href=\"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0545.tlg002.perseus-grc2:2.33/\" target=\"_blank\">Aelian, Varia Historia 2.33\u003C/a>, conjectured that the base may have supported the ivory statue of the river-god Akragas said to have been dedicated at Delphi by the Akragantines in commemoration of the advent of democracy in 471 BCE. Both historical identifications remain conjectural. Bousquet distinguished this smaller base from the other Akragantine dedication at Delphi, inv. 5098 (Dubois 182b).\u003C/p>  ",{"id":261,"html":262},"bibliography","\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Bousquet 1959 149–150, fig. 4 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001375\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001375\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> De Waele 1971 39–40 no. 8, pl. 10 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002040\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002040\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Lazzarini 1976 905 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002517\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002517\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Dubois 1989 182a \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000187\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000187\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Jeffery and Johnston 1990 Addenda, 372 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000678\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000678\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Arena 2002 94 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001373\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001373\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  ",{"id":264,"html":265},"license"," Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. ",[267,269,272,273],{"html":268},"Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa",{"id":270,"lang":114,"html":271},"edition-interpretive","\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[Ἀ]κραγαντῖνοι τ[ο͂ι \u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"divine\" data-text=\"Ἀπό\n                    λο̄νι\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἀπό\n                    λο̄νι\">Ἀπό-]\u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>λο̄νι\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\">(vac.)\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",{"html":268},{"id":274,"lang":114,"html":275},"edition-diplomatic","\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[.]ΚΡΑΓΑΝΤΙΝΟΙΤ[...\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"divine\" data-text=\"Ἀπό\n                    λο̄νι\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἀπό\n                    λο̄νι\">...]\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>ΛΟ̄ΝΙ\u003C/span>\u003C/span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; \u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",[],[278],{"html":57},"\u003C?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003C?xml-model href=\"https://epidoc.stoa.org/schema/latest/tei-epidoc.rng\" type=\"application/xml\" schematypens=\"http://relaxng.org/ns/structure/1.0\"?>\n\u003C?xml-model href=\"../schematron/ircyr-checking.sch\" schematypens=\"http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron\"?>\n\u003CTEI xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xml:lang=\"en\" xmlns:xi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude\">\n    \u003CteiHeader>\n        \u003CfileDesc>\n            \u003CtitleStmt>\n                \u003Ctitle>Dedication by the Akragantines to Apollo at Delphi\u003C/title>\n                \u003Ceditor ref=\"#JP\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/editor>\n                \u003Cprincipal ref=\"#VM\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/principal>\n                \u003Cfunder>John Fell OUP Research Fund\u003C/funder>\n                \u003Cfunder>\u003Cref target=\"https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/885040\">ERC Advanced Grant no.885040\u003C/ref>\u003C/funder>\n                \u003CrespStmt>\n                    \u003Cname xml:id=\"JP\" ref=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/name>\n                    \u003Cresp>Project direction, template development, general editing\u003C/resp>\n                \u003C/respStmt>\n                \u003CrespStmt>\n                    \u003Cname xml:id=\"SS\" ref=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3914-9569\">Simona Stoyanova\u003C/name>\n                    \u003Cresp>Standardisation of template and tidying up encoding\u003C/resp>\n                \u003C/respStmt>\n                \u003CrespStmt>\n                    \u003Cname xml:id=\"VM\" ref=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/name>\n                    \u003Cresp>Bibliographic research, metadata, editing and EpiDoc encoding\u003C/resp>\n                \u003C/respStmt>\n            \u003C/titleStmt>\n            \u003CpublicationStmt>\n                \u003Cauthority>I.Sicily\u003C/authority>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"filename\">ISic004523\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"TM\">931438\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"EDR\"/>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"EDH\"/>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"EDCS\"/>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"PHI\">329476\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"URI\">http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic004523\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"DOI\"/>\n                \u003Cavailability>\n                    \u003Clicence target=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\">Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence.\u003C/licence>\n                \u003C/availability>\n            \u003C/publicationStmt>\n            \u003CsourceDesc>\n                \u003CmsDesc>\n                    \u003CmsIdentifier>\n                        \u003Ccountry>Greece\u003C/country>\n                        \u003Cregion>Phocis\u003C/region>\n                        \u003Csettlement>Delphi\u003C/settlement>\n                        \u003Crepository role=\"museum\">Archaeological Museum of Delphi\u003C/repository>\n                        \u003Cidno type=\"inventory\">7262\u003C/idno>\n                        \u003CaltIdentifier>\n                            \u003Csettlement/>\n                            \u003Crepository/>\n                            \u003Cidno type=\"old\"/>\n                        \u003C/altIdentifier>\n                    \u003C/msIdentifier>\n                    \u003CmsContents>\n                        \u003CtextLang mainLang=\"grc\">Ancient Greek\u003C/textLang>\n                    \u003C/msContents>\n                    \u003CphysDesc>\n                        \u003CobjectDesc>\n                            \u003CsupportDesc>\n                                \u003Csupport>\n                                    \u003Cp>Limestone base, broken on the right and at the back, with a smooth left side. No recognisable setting traces survive on the upper bed.\u003C/p>\n                                    \u003Cmaterial ana=\"#material.stone.limestone\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/66.html\">limestone\u003C/material>\n                                    \u003CobjectType ana=\"#object.base\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/57.html\">base\u003C/objectType>\n                                    \u003Cdimensions>\n                                        \u003Cheight unit=\"cm\">31.5\u003C/height>\n                                        \u003Cwidth unit=\"cm\" atMost=\"40\">40\u003C/width>\n                                        \u003Cdepth unit=\"cm\" atMost=\"35\">35\u003C/depth>\n                                    \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003C/support>\n                                \u003Ccondition ana=\"#condition.fragment\"/>\n                            \u003C/supportDesc>\n                            \u003ClayoutDesc>\n                                \u003Clayout>\n                                    \u003Cp>The text is arranged over two lines, with almost no interlinear space.\u003C/p>\n                                    \u003Crs ana=\"#execution.chiselled\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1\">chiselled\u003C/rs>\n                                    \u003Cdamage ana=\"#text_condition.incomplete\"/>\n                                \u003C/layout>\n                            \u003C/layoutDesc>\n                        \u003C/objectDesc>\n                        \u003ChandDesc>\n                            \u003ChandNote>\n                                \u003Cp>Bousquet notes rho with a triangular loop and a tail, alpha with an oblique crossbar descending to the foot of the right hasta, lunate sigma, and nu with an oblique left hasta and an almost vertical right hasta.\u003C/p>\n                                \u003Clocus from=\"line1\" to=\"line2\">Lines 1–2\u003C/locus>\n                                \u003Cdimensions type=\"letterHeight\">\n                                    \u003Cheight unit=\"mm\" atLeast=\"18\" atMost=\"21\">18–21\u003C/height>\n                                \u003C/dimensions>\n                            \u003C/handNote>\n                        \u003C/handDesc>\n                    \u003C/physDesc>\n                    \u003Chistory>\n                        \u003Corigin>\n                            \u003CorigPlace>\n                                \u003Cregion>Sicilia\u003C/region>\n                                \u003CplaceName type=\"ancient\" ref=\"http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462086\">Agrigentum\u003C/placeName>\n                                \u003CplaceName type=\"modern\" ref=\"http://sws.geonames.org/6541860\">Agrigento\u003C/placeName>\n                                \u003Cgeo>37.32084, 13.58876\u003C/geo>\n                            \u003C/origPlace>\n                            \u003CorigDate datingMethod=\"#julian\" notBefore-custom=\"-0475\" notAfter-custom=\"-0450\" evidence=\"lettering\">Second quarter of the 5th century BCE (tentative)\u003C/origDate>\n                        \u003C/origin>\n                        \u003Cprovenance type=\"found\" subtype=\"discovered\" when=\"1951-07-20\">Found reused in a wall of late date east of the East Baths at \u003CplaceName ref=\"https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/540726\">Delphi\u003C/placeName>, Greece.\u003Cgeo cert=\"medium\">38.482289, 22.501169\u003C/geo>\u003C/provenance>\n                        \u003C!-- representative coordinates for Delphi, not the precise findspot -->\n                        \u003Cprovenance type=\"observed\" subtype=\"autopsied\">None\u003C/provenance>\n                    \u003C/history>\n                \u003C/msDesc>\n            \u003C/sourceDesc>\n        \u003C/fileDesc>\n        \u003CencodingDesc>\n            \u003Cp>Encoded following the latest EpiDoc guidelines\u003C/p>\n            \u003Cxi:include href=\"../alists/ISicily-taxonomies.xml\">\n                \u003Cxi:fallback>\n                    \u003Cp>Taxonomies for ISicily controlled values\u003C/p>\n                \u003C/xi:fallback>\n            \u003C/xi:include>\n            \u003Cxi:include href=\"../alists/charDecl.xml\">\n                \u003Cxi:fallback>\n                    \u003Cp>ISicily glyphs authority list\u003C/p>\n                \u003C/xi:fallback>\n            \u003C/xi:include>\n        \u003C/encodingDesc>\n        \u003CprofileDesc>\n            \u003CcalendarDesc>\n                \u003Ccalendar xml:id=\"julian\">\n                    \u003Cp>Julian Calendar\u003C/p>\n                \u003C/calendar>\n            \u003C/calendarDesc>\n            \u003ClangUsage>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"en\">English\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"it\">Italian\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"grc\">Ancient Greek\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"la\">Latin\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"he\">Hebrew\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"phn\">Phoenician\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"xpu\">Punic\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"osc\">Oscan\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"xly\">Elymian\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"scx\">Sikel\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"sxc\">Sikan\u003C/language>\n            \u003C/langUsage>\n            \u003CtextClass>\n                \u003Ckeywords scheme=\"https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription\">\n                    \u003Cterm ana=\"#function.dedication\" ref=\"https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription/Dedication\">dedication\u003C/term>\n                \u003C/keywords>\n            \u003C/textClass>\n        \u003C/profileDesc>\n        \u003CrevisionDesc status=\"draft\">\n            \u003ClistChange>\n                \u003Cchange when=\"2026-07-30\" who=\"#VM\">Creation of file and EpiDoc encoding from published sources\u003C/change>\n            \u003C/listChange>\n        \u003C/revisionDesc>\n    \u003C/teiHeader>\n    \u003Cfacsimile>\u003Csurface/>\u003C!--\n        \u003Csurface type=\"front\">\n            \u003Cgraphic n=\"screen\" url=\"ISic004523_tiled.tif\" height=\"3680px\" width=\"5520px\">\n                \u003Cdesc>I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana\u003C/desc>\n            \u003C/graphic>\n            \u003Cgraphic n=\"print\" url=\"ISic004523.jpg\" height=\"3680px\" width=\"5520px\">\n                \u003Cdesc>I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana\u003C/desc>\n            \u003C/graphic>\n         \u003C/surface>\n     -->\u003C/facsimile>\n    \u003Ctext>\n        \u003Cbody>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"edition\" subtype=\"primary\" xml:space=\"preserve\" xml:lang=\"grc\" resp=\"#VM\">\n                \u003Cab>\n                    \u003Clb n=\"1\"/>\u003CplaceName type=\"ethnic\">\u003Csupplied reason=\"lost\">Ἀ\u003C/supplied>κραγαντῖνοι\u003C/placeName> τ\u003Csupplied reason=\"lost\">ο͂ι\u003C/supplied> \u003CpersName type=\"divine\">\u003Cname>\u003Csupplied reason=\"lost\">Ἀπό\u003C/supplied>\n                    \u003Clb n=\"2\" break=\"no\"/>λο̄νι\u003C/name>\u003C/persName> \u003Cspace extent=\"unknown\" unit=\"character\"/>\n                \u003C/ab>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"apparatus\">\n                \u003ClistApp>\n                    \u003Capp>\n                        \u003Cnote>Text after Arena 2002 (IGASMG II² 94).\u003C/note>\n                    \u003C/app>\n                    \u003Capp loc=\"lines 1–2\">\n                        \u003Cnote>Arena prints the dialectal form Ἀπόλο̄νι and regularises it as Ἀπόλλωνι.\u003C/note>\n                    \u003C/app>\n                    \u003Capp loc=\"lines 1–2\">\n                        \u003Cnote>Because the original width of the base cannot be established, the restoration remains uncertain. Dubois 1989 records the alternatives τ[ῶι Ἀπόλ]λωνι and τ[ὸ ἄγαλμα τῶι Ἀπόλ]λωνι; Arena 2002 adopts the former.\u003C/note>\n                    \u003C/app>\n                \u003C/listApp>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"translation\" xml:lang=\"en\" resp=\"#VM\">\n                \u003Cp>The Akragantines [dedicated this] to Apollo.\u003C/p>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"commentary\">\n                \u003Cp>Bousquet tentatively dated the dedication to the second quarter of the 5th century BCE and suggested a connection with the \n                    establishment of democracy at Akragas after the fall of the tyranny and the death of Theron in 472 BCE. De Waele, drawing on \n                    \u003Cref target=\"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0545.tlg002.perseus-grc2:2.33/\">Aelian, Varia Historia 2.33\u003C/ref>, \n                    conjectured that the base may have supported the ivory statue of the river-god Akragas said to have \n                    been dedicated at Delphi by the Akragantines in commemoration of the advent of democracy in 471 BCE. Both historical \n                    identifications remain conjectural. Bousquet distinguished this smaller base from the other Akragantine dedication at Delphi, \n                    inv. 5098 (Dubois 182b).\u003C/p>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"bibliography\">\n                \u003ClistBibl type=\"edition\">\n                    \u003Cbibl>\n                        \u003Cauthor>Bousquet\u003C/author>\n                        \u003Cdate>1959\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>149–150, fig. 4\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"http://zotero.org/groups/382445/items/VB5QSXQK\"/>\n                        \u003Cref target=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001375\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001375\u003C/ref>\n                    \u003C/bibl>\n                    \u003Cbibl>\n                        \u003Cauthor>De Waele\u003C/author>\n                        \u003Cdate>1971\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>39–40 no. 8, pl. 10\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"http://zotero.org/groups/382445/items/CXHAXNBQ\"/>\n                        \u003Cref target=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002040\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002040\u003C/ref>\n                    \u003C/bibl>\n                    \u003Cbibl>\n                        \u003Cauthor>Lazzarini\u003C/author>\n                        \u003Cdate>1976\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>905\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"http://zotero.org/groups/382445/items/3N7Z6QX5\"/>\n                        \u003Cref target=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002517\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002517\u003C/ref>\n                    \u003C/bibl>\n                    \u003Cbibl type=\"corpus\" n=\"IGDS\">\n                        \u003Cauthor>Dubois\u003C/author>\n                        \u003Cdate>1989\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>182a\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"http://zotero.org/groups/382445/items/RWXNUFEX\"/>\n                        \u003Cref target=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000187\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000187\u003C/ref>\n                    \u003C/bibl>\n                    \u003Cbibl type=\"corpus\" n=\"LSAG\">\n                        \u003Cauthor>Jeffery and Johnston\u003C/author>\n                        \u003Cdate>1990\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>Addenda, 372\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"http://zotero.org/groups/382445/items/QUWGZA84\"/>\n                        \u003Cref target=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000678\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000678\u003C/ref>\n                    \u003C/bibl>\n                    \u003Cbibl type=\"corpus\" n=\"IGASMG II²\">\n                        \u003Cauthor>Arena\u003C/author>\n                        \u003Cdate>2002\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>94\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"http://zotero.org/groups/382445/items/65P7AM6N\"/>\n                        \u003Cref target=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001373\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001373\u003C/ref>\n                    \u003C/bibl>\n                \u003C/listBibl>\n                \u003ClistBibl type=\"discussion\">\n                    \u003Cbibl/>\n                \u003C/listBibl>\n            \u003C/div>\n        \u003C/body>\n    \u003C/text>\n\u003C/TEI>"],"uses":{"params":["slug"]}}]}
